<div class="page">
  <h1 class="page-title">Philosophy</h1>
  <p class="page-subtitle">How I think about building software, leading teams, and solving problems that matter.</p>

  <article class="section-gap">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Simplicity Is Leverage</h2>
    <p class="prose">The best systems I've worked on are easy to explain. Not because they're trivial, but because they're intentional. Complexity is not strength. Simplicity, earned through understanding, is.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="section-gap">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Organizations Fail Before Technology Does</h2>
    <p class="prose">Engineering organizations don't fail because of technology. They fail because their structures, incentives, and communication patterns can't support the systems they build. Fix the organization and the technology follows.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="section-gap">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Progressive Influence Over Declarative Authority</h2>
    <p class="prose">Lasting change doesn't come from mandates. It comes from demonstrating value, building trust, and making the right path the easy path. Influence compounds. Authority depletes.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="section-gap">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Make Big Problems Small Problems</h2>
    <p class="prose">Every insurmountable challenge is a collection of tractable ones. Break things down. Find the seams. Solve the smallest meaningful piece first, then let momentum carry the rest.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="section-gap">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Raise the Bar, Don't Guard the Gate</h2>
    <p class="prose">Engineering excellence isn't about exclusion. It's about creating systems, patterns, and cultures that lift everyone's work. Mentor generously. Document intentionally. Build platforms that multiply capability.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="section-gap">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Kindness as Engineering Practice</h2>
    <p class="prose">Being known for kindness is not weakness. Kind teams share knowledge freely, give honest feedback without cruelty, and build trust that survives hard decisions.</p>
  </article>

  <hr class="divider-line" />

  <h2 class="sidebar-heading">Things I Believe</h2>
  <ul class="belief-list">
    <li class="belief-item">Good systems leave room to evolve.</li>
    <li class="belief-item">The cost of complexity is cognitive, not just technical.</li>
    <li class="belief-item">Familiarity is not the same as fitness.</li>
    <li class="belief-item">Data grounds discussions. Intuition starts them.</li>
    <li class="belief-item">Clever code is a liability. Boring code is a gift to your future self.</li>
    <li class="belief-item">Don't give technical solutions to people problems.</li>
    <li class="belief-item">Other folks are amazing. Be the shadow that makes their light clearer.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
